{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>When you finish tithing all the tithe of your produce in the third year.</b> When you finish separating the tithes of the third year. He fixed the time of removal and declaration on the eve of Passover of the fourth year, as it says ״מִקְצֵה שָׁלֹשׁ שָׁנִים תּוֹצִיא וגו״׳ (Deuteronomy 14). It says here ״מִקֵּץ,״ and it says below ״מִקֵּץ שֶׁבַע שָׁנִים״ regarding Hakhel (Deuteronomy 31) — just as there it is a festival, so here it is a festival. If you say: just as there it is the festival of Sukkot, so here too it is the festival of Sukkot — Scripture says <b>when you finish tithing</b> the tithes of the third year: a festival on which the tithes are completed, and that is Passover, for there are many trees whose fruit is gathered after Sukkot. It turns out that the tithes of the third year are completed on Passover of the fourth year, and anyone who delayed his tithes — Scripture required him to remove them from the house (ibid. 5)." "<b>The year of the tithe.</b> A year in which only one tithe is practiced, of the two tithes that were practiced in the two years preceding it — for the first year of the shemittah cycle has first tithe, as it says ״כִּי תִקְחוּ מֵאֵת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת הַמַּעֲשֵׂר״ (Numbers 18), and second tithe, as it says ״וְאָכַלְתָּ לִפְנֵי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ … מַעְשַׂר דְּגָנְךָ תִּירֹשְׁךָ וְיִצְהָרֶךָ״ (Deuteronomy 14) — here are two tithes. And it comes and teaches you here, in the third year, that of those two tithes only one is practiced — and which one? This is first tithe. And in place of second tithe he gives poor man's tithe, as it says here <b>and you shall give to the Levi</b> what is his — here is first tithe; <b>to the stranger, the orphan, and the widow</b> — this is poor man's tithe (cf. Sifrei)." "<b>And they shall eat within your gates and be satisfied.</b> Give them enough for their satisfaction. From here the Sages said: one does not give the poor person at the threshing floor less than a half-kav of wheat, etc. (Sifrei; Jerusalem Talmud Pe'ah 8:8)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:32.459691378Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}